#
# Counter-example for math:SlotIndexUniquenessShape: two math:argumentSlot cells of one
# binder share math:slotIndex 0, so operand order is ambiguous. Each slot is otherwise
# well-formed (index + expression), isolating the SPARQL uniqueness violation. Validation
# MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent (math:DuplicateArgumentSlotIndex). Bound by
# ex:ecSlotIndexDuplicate.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:badBinder a math:BindingExpression ;
    math:operator math:summationBinder ;
    math:boundVariable ex:kDecl ;
    math:argumentSlot ex:badSlotA , ex:badSlotB .

ex:badSlotA a math:ArgumentSlot ; math:slotIndex 0 ; math:slotExpression ex:exprA .
ex:badSlotB a math:ArgumentSlot ; math:slotIndex 0 ; math:slotExpression ex:exprB .

ex:exprA a math:MathematicalExpression .
ex:exprB a math:MathematicalExpression .
ex:kDecl a math:VariableDeclaration .
